  "supported_context": "Linux x64, edition 2024, embed-bitcode=no and opt-level=0. Native builds accept debuginfo=0. Dependency-free executables additionally accept unsplit and unstripped full Rust debug information using the native LLVM emitter and Clang. The debug emitter represents scalar values, selected aggregates and variants, references, function pointers and local bindings across normal control flow. Scalar leaf libraries and executables without Cargo dependencies also link with the unwind panic strategy and actual unwind ranges. Linked artifacts with dependencies require panic=abort. Metadata-only checks also accept the ordinary Cargo dev profile with unwind, debuginfo=2 and the optional incremental cache location. Checked scalar signatures carry every integer type. Linked artifacts require the existing direct ABI for 32-bit, 64-bit and pointer-sized integers. Cargo library checks and builds may use one direct scalar leaf dependency supplied as metadata. Cargo executable checks use a closed scalar metadata graph. Executable builds additionally use the matching archives. Executable dep-info covers source files and actual include and environment reads from the native resolver and expander. The admitted extern lint uses native checked reads. Dependency-free Cargo unit and integration tests with the unwind strategy link the pinned Rust libtest runtime and keep body checking and emission in Lust. Tests may use the supported native main return forms.",
  "request_options": "LibraryOptions is per request, outside native SessionKey and Client. At O0, omitted overflow-checks inherits the effective debug-assertions setting; admitted explicit values take precedence. The direct Rust adapter preserves last-option precedence, while the bounded Cargo artifact adapter preserves debug level (-g and -C debuginfo), split and strip precedence. Other duplicate codegen options are refused. Debug choices travel on public requests outside the semantic session key. Native executable debug requests use full unsplit Rust DWARF for the represented source and types. Other debug levels and split sidecars remain unimplemented for linked output. Unstable embedding None/true/false are distinct metadata/SVH variants; effective None/true use full archive metadata and false uses its matching header stub. Force-warn/JSON do not enter the metadata hash. Stable -C embed-metadata remains unrepresented.",
  "artifact_variants": "At most three embedding choices for the current native link snapshot, plus the last durable link publication. The metadata-only cache holds a single checked generation and requires no native object, export, or archive work.",
  "semantic_owner": "One existing native prepare/emit continuation; only existing completed scalar declarations/bodies.",
  "unimplemented": [
    "default-profile linked libraries and dependent executables",
    "wider Rust source-level debug information",
    "general Rust panic cleanup and exception semantics",
    "stable -C embed-metadata and wider unstable options",
    "general native library and executable dependency graphs",
    "wider native completion",
    "other targets/profiles",
    "socket-free public retained host"
  ],
  "inactive_history": "Owner-start budget, default 128 entries and 16 MiB of known payload per native-object, native-definition and artifact cache; current/published/in-flight evidence protected. Lowering the real entry limit exercises the same LRU cut. Actual RSS includes live source, allocator overhead and original native caches.",
  "publication": "All bytes staged/synced before replacements; complete files replace in metadata/dep-info/archive order. Partial multi-name effects and uncertain durability are terminal. No-op exact output bytes leave output inodes/mtimes unchanged.",
  "runtime_limitation": "The pinned dynamic llvm-ar/llvm-objcopy dependency closure may require the exact 208,283,952-byte LLVM shared library. This is artifact-tool closure, not a proved minimal source cut or compiler speed qualification.",
